{
    "background_story": "Myra was a tiny Eastern Pewee who lived in a cozy nest near a babbling brook. Despite her small size, she had a big personality and a beautiful singing voice. Every morning, Myra would perch on a branch overlooking the water and sing her heart out, filling the air with sweet melodies. Her songs were so enchanting that they attracted a variety of birds and animals to the area, creating a thriving community. Myra's tiny size belied her fierce protectiveness of her home and family. She would fearlessly chase away predators, squawking loudly to defend her territory. Her bravery and loyalty earned her the respect and admiration of her fellow creatures, who looked up to her as a leader and a symbol of resilience.",
